# Release notes for CurseForge, Wago and the GitHub release.
#
# Without this the packager writes its own notes from the git log. Our commit
# messages are German by house rule and ASCII transliterated, so every release
# shipped notes that read like typos to anyone outside this repo, while the
# English changelog only ever reached Discord and the in-game patch notes.
#
# CHANGELOG-release.md holds the newest version's section only, and is written
# by tools/gen_changelog.js alongside Modules/ChangelogData.lua -- so the three
# places that show release notes all come from the same source.
#
# Careful: the packager falls back to the git log SILENTLY when the file is
# missing or stale, so a release that forgot to run the generator would quietly
# go back to German. tools/check.js compares it against CHANGELOG.md and fails
# the build before that can reach a distribution site.
#
# Deliberately no "ignore" list. Without one the packager keeps its default file
# selection, so the only change to the shipped zip is CHANGELOG-release.md
# itself riding along -- a few hundred bytes. Ignoring it was tempting, but it
# is unclear whether the packager still finds a manual changelog it was told to
# leave out, and a wrong guess there breaks releasing, not just tidiness.
manual-changelog:
    filename: CHANGELOG-release.md
    markup-type: markdown
